{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he said</b> — <b>and the bowl</b>: like the bowl of [the altar's] ascent. Now I shall tell you the gist of this matter briefly, for the prophet afterward mentioned all its details: there were two olive trees, one on the right and the bowl on the left; and the olive clusters fall from the trees onto two golden spouts, and from these they drip and are pressed, and pure oil is made like gold, and they pour it into the bowl. And in the bowl were seven receptacles — seven lamps and seven receptacles — and behold seven once more, like [flowing] to the outer court to the people. And the angel explained the meaning of this vision." "<b>Not by might and not by power</b>: just as I saw the oil produced and burning on its own, so the House will be built — not by the great power that Zerubbabel has nor by the multitude of his strength, but by the spirit of HaShem and His aid."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The text appears to sketch the vision's mechanics in compressed, rapid fashion; rendered hyper-literally. 'גלה' taken as 'גולה' (bowl) per the lemma. The repeated 'שבעה' counting and the phrase 'כמו אל החצר החיצונה' are obscure and translated as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:55.508232884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}